#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290959aa-c9e0-552a-b454-bf5b41e57491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673196} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0b566c-e3b7-52ff-95cf-90860925fada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673208}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673208} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e751ad0-31b9-5191-b323-5b7b0e2bc46c" :answer-field/key "$A\\text{ is not invertible}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b15f975-67ea-5476-8f03-c7f74f2dc017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673205} {:answer/id #uuid "8bebcac0-8f6e-5792-b15e-d22a8c0de5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673214}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673214} :answer-field/id #uuid "460aa660-c8cb-5c14-a7a7-344c954cf7ea" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475b0073-903b-5909-957b-c2bf958a0e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673203} {:answer/id #uuid "f14c2be7-6d66-59ed-8e7e-b0e8ed2d34b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673203} :answer-field/id #uuid "62ecaf89-7f8c-5743-8190-377e5b4987a1" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\mid {x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + {x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ is true. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ only."}]}
